    <paragraph>A non-negative function is a probability density function if it satisfies the following definition: $$\lbrack 0,\infty)$$ The probability that a random variable x lies between a and b is given by $$F(s) = {\int_{0}^{\infty}{e^{-sx}f(x)dx}}$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="406" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Show that $$f(x) = 1$$ is a probability density function.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="407" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the probability that x is between 0 and 0.3. (Use the function defined in the preceding problem.) Use four-place decimal accuracy.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>0.8775</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
